    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3 Objects of this Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.7",
      "values:originalText": "The main objects of this Act are:\n(a) to establish an apolitical public service that is efficient and\neffective in serving the Government, the Parliament and the\nAustralian public; and\n(b) to provide a legal framework for the effective and fair\nemployment, management and leadership of APS employees;\nand\n(c) to define the powers, functions and responsibilities of\nAgency Heads, the Australian Public Service Commissioner\nand the Merit Protection Commissioner; and\n(d) to establish rights and obligations of APS employees.",
      "skos:definition": "The main objects of this Act are:\n(a) to establish an apolitical public service that is efficient and\neffective in serving the Government, the Parliament and the\nAustralian public; and\n(b) to provide a legal framework for the effective and fair\nemployment, management and leadership of APS employees;\nand\n(c) to define the powers, functions and responsibilities of\nAgency Heads, the Australian Public Service Commissioner\nand the Merit Protection Commissioner; and\n(d) to establish rights and obligations of APS employees.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-3-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "eadcf296cba0aaf31486e86a6c41379ff4b195d8550fca77fb57dd5ff93e0ef3",
      "skos:note": "Establishes main objects of the Act"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3 Objects of this Act",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 7,
      "values:originalText": "The main objects of this Act are:\n(a) to establish an apolitical public service that is efficient and\neffective in serving the Government, the Parliament and the\nAustralian public; and\n(b) to provide a legal framework for the effective and fair\nemployment, management and leadership of APS employees;\nand\n(c) to define the powers, functions and responsibilities of\nAgency Heads, the Australian Public Service Commissioner\nand the Merit Protection Commissioner; and\n(d) to establish rights and obligations of APS employees."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-3"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6 Engagement of employees in Department or Executive Agency",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "(1) All persons engaged on behalf of the Commonwealth as employees\nto perform functions in a Department or Executive Agency must be\nengaged under this Act, or under the authority of another Act.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to persons engaged on an honorary\nbasis.\n(3) This section does not, by implication, affect any power that an\nAgency Head might otherwise have to engage persons as\nindependent contractors.\n\n\nInterpretation  Part 2\n\nSection 7\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024",
      "skos:definition": "(1) All persons engaged on behalf of the Commonwealth as employees\nto perform functions in a Department or Executive Agency must be\nengaged under this Act, or under the authority of another Act.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to persons engaged on an honorary\nbasis.\n(3) This section does not, by implication, affect any power that an\nAgency Head might otherwise have to engage persons as\nindependent contractors.\n\n\nInterpretation  Part 2\n\nSection 7\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-6-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-6-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-6-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b1bdf2a7e9611f29f406c940fde6918a701c201360ce3bdcbce61359fbe52164"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6 Engagement of employees in Department or Executive Agency",
