      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-6-ss-3-logic-deontic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Permission",
      "cml:logicSummary": "This section permits Agency Head to engage persons as independent contractors despite its obligation.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(3) This section does not, by implication, affect any power that an Agency Head might otherwise have to engage persons as independent contractors.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "This section permits Agency Head to engage persons as independent contractors despite its obligation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-7",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "7 Interpretation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-7"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.9",
      "values:originalText": "In this Act, unless the contrary intention appears:\nacting SES employee means a non-SES employee who is acting in\na position usually occupied by an SES employee.\nAgency means:\n(a) a Department; or\n(b) an Executive Agency; or\n(c) a Statutory Agency.\nAgency Head means:\n(a) the Secretary of a Department; or\n(b) the Head of an Executive Agency; or\n(c) the Head of a Statutory Agency.\nAgency Minister means:\n(a) in relation to a Department—the Minister who administers\nthe Department; or\n(b) in relation to an Executive Agency—the Minister who\nadministers the Agency; or\n(c) in relation to a Statutory Agency—the Minister who\nadministers the provision of the Act that provides for the\nappointment of the Head of the Agency.\nAgency website means a website maintained by an Agency.\nAPS means the Australian Public Service established by section 9.\nAPS employee means:\n(a) a person engaged under section 22; or\n(b) a person who is engaged as an APS employee under\nsection 72.",
      "skos:definition": "In this Act, unless the contrary intention appears:\nacting SES employee means a non-SES employee who is acting in\na position usually occupied by an SES employee.\nAgency means:\n(a) a Department; or\n(b) an Executive Agency; or\n(c) a Statutory Agency.\nAgency Head means:\n(a) the Secretary of a Department; or\n(b) the Head of an Executive Agency; or\n(c) the Head of a Statutory Agency.\nAgency Minister means:\n(a) in relation to a Department—the Minister who administers\nthe Department; or\n(b) in relation to an Executive Agency—the Minister who\nadministers the Agency; or\n(c) in relation to a Statutory Agency—the Minister who\nadministers the provision of the Act that provides for the\nappointment of the Head of the Agency.\nAgency website means a website maintained by an Agency.\nAPS means the Australian Public Service established by section 9.\nAPS employee means:\n(a) a person engaged under section 22; or\n(b) a person who is engaged as an APS employee under\nsection 72.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-7-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-7-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-7-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-7-logic-descriptionlogic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-7-logic-descriptionlogic-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b56062c390c8503ed82808ac604c997d4460c0076a69767d530d552b43d5d257",
      "skos:note": "Definitions for SES employee, Agency, and APS employee."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-7",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "7 Interpretation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 9,
      "values:originalText": "In this Act, unless the contrary intention appears:\nacting SES employee means a non-SES employee who is acting in\na position usually occupied by an SES employee.\nAgency means:\n(a) a Department; or\n(b) an Executive Agency; or\n(c) a Statutory Agency.\nAgency Head means:\n(a) the Secretary of a Department; or\n(b) the Head of an Executive Agency; or\n(c) the Head of a Statutory Agency.\nAgency Minister means:\n(a) in relation to a Department—the Minister who administers\nthe Department; or\n(b) in relation to an Executive Agency—the Minister who\nadministers the Agency; or\n(c) in relation to a Statutory Agency—the Minister who\nadministers the provision of the Act that provides for the\nappointment of the Head of the Agency.\nAgency website means a website maintained by an Agency.\nAPS means the Australian Public Service established by section 9.\nAPS employee means:\n(a) a person engaged under section 22; or\n(b) a person who is engaged as an APS employee under\nsection 72."
    },
