    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-10a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10A APS Employment Principles",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-10a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.15",
      "values:originalText": "APS Employment Principles\n(1) The APS is a career-based public service that:\n(a) makes fair employment decisions with a fair system of\nreview; and\n(b) recognises that the usual basis for engagement is as an\nongoing APS employee; and\n(c) makes decisions relating to engagement and promotion that\nare based on merit; and\n(d) requires effective performance from each employee; and\n(e) provides flexible, safe and rewarding workplaces where\ncommunication, consultation, cooperation and input from\nemployees on matters that affect their workplaces are valued;\nand\n(f) provides workplaces that are free from discrimination,\npatronage and favouritism; and\n(g) recognises the diversity of the Australian community and\nfosters diversity in the workplace.\nDecisions based on merit\n(2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(c), a decision relating to\nengagement or promotion is based on merit if:\n(a) all eligible members of the community were given a\nreasonable opportunity to apply to perform the relevant\nduties; and\n(b) an assessment is made of the relative suitability of the\ncandidates to perform the relevant duties, using a competitive\nselection process; and",
      "skos:definition": "APS Employment Principles\n(1) The APS is a career-based public service that:\n(a) makes fair employment decisions with a fair system of\nreview; and\n(b) recognises that the usual basis for engagement is as an\nongoing APS employee; and\n(c) makes decisions relating to engagement and promotion that\nare based on merit; and\n(d) requires effective performance from each employee; and\n(e) provides flexible, safe and rewarding workplaces where\ncommunication, consultation, cooperation and input from\nemployees on matters that affect their workplaces are valued;\nand\n(f) provides workplaces that are free from discrimination,\npatronage and favouritism; and\n(g) recognises the diversity of the Australian community and\nfosters diversity in the workplace.\nDecisions based on merit\n(2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(c), a decision relating to\nengagement or promotion is based on merit if:\n(a) all eligible members of the community were given a\nreasonable opportunity to apply to perform the relevant\nduties; and\n(b) an assessment is made of the relative suitability of the\ncandidates to perform the relevant duties, using a competitive\nselection process; and",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-10a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-10a-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4920f0cab8b746ff9a5d8f8fae9b35805465a74c1b04cf61b0ce0bce13cab46d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-10a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10A APS Employment Principles",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 15,
      "values:originalText": "APS Employment Principles\n(1) The APS is a career-based public service that:\n(a) makes fair employment decisions with a fair system of\nreview; and\n(b) recognises that the usual basis for engagement is as an\nongoing APS employee; and\n(c) makes decisions relating to engagement and promotion that\nare based on merit; and\n(d) requires effective performance from each employee; and\n(e) provides flexible, safe and rewarding workplaces where\ncommunication, consultation, cooperation and input from\nemployees on matters that affect their workplaces are valued;\nand\n(f) provides workplaces that are free from discrimination,\npatronage and favouritism; and\n(g) recognises the diversity of the Australian community and\nfosters diversity in the workplace.\nDecisions based on merit\n(2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(c), a decision relating to\nengagement or promotion is based on merit if:\n(a) all eligible members of the community were given a\nreasonable opportunity to apply to perform the relevant\nduties; and\n(b) an assessment is made of the relative suitability of the\ncandidates to perform the relevant duties, using a competitive\nselection process; and"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-10a-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10A(1) APS Employment Principles",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-10a-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.15",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The APS is a career-based public service that:\n(a) makes fair employment decisions with a fair system of\nreview; and\n(b) recognises that the usual basis for engagement is as an\nongoing APS employee; and\n(c) makes decisions relating to engagement and promotion that\nare based on merit; and\n(d) requires effective performance from each employee; and\n(e) provides flexible, safe and rewarding workplaces where\ncommunication, consultation, cooperation and input from\nemployees on matters that affect their workplaces are valued;\nand\n(f) provides workplaces that are free from discrimination,\npatronage and favouritism; and\n(g) recognises the diversity of the Australian community and\nfosters diversity in the workplace.\nDecisions based on merit",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The APS is a career-based public service that:\n(a) makes fair employment decisions with a fair system of\nreview; and\n(b) recognises that the usual basis for engagement is as an\nongoing APS employee; and\n(c) makes decisions relating to engagement and promotion that\nare based on merit; and\n(d) requires effective performance from each employee; and\n(e) provides flexible, safe and rewarding workplaces where\ncommunication, consultation, cooperation and input from\nemployees on matters that affect their workplaces are valued;\nand\n(f) provides workplaces that are free from discrimination,\npatronage and favouritism; and\n(g) recognises the diversity of the Australian community and\nfosters diversity in the workplace.\nDecisions based on merit",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-10a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-10a-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-10a-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        },
