    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-10a-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10A(2) APS Employment Principles",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-10a-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.15",
      "values:originalText": "(2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(c), a decision relating to\nengagement or promotion is based on merit if:\n(a) all eligible members of the community were given a\nreasonable opportunity to apply to perform the relevant\nduties; and\n(b) an assessment is made of the relative suitability of the\ncandidates to perform the relevant duties, using a competitive\nselection process; and",
      "skos:definition": "(2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(c), a decision relating to\nengagement or promotion is based on merit if:\n(a) all eligible members of the community were given a\nreasonable opportunity to apply to perform the relevant\nduties; and\n(b) an assessment is made of the relative suitability of the\ncandidates to perform the relevant duties, using a competitive\nselection process; and",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-10a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-10a-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-10a-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7c80f1ac47484fca7faab46a9aced46647eb14543586ade5423b16ee12289c14",
      "skos:note": "Decision based on merit for engagement or promotion"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-10a-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10A(2) APS Employment Principles",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 15,
      "values:originalText": "(2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(c), a decision relating to\nengagement or promotion is based on merit if:\n(a) all eligible members of the community were given a\nreasonable opportunity to apply to perform the relevant\nduties; and\n(b) an assessment is made of the relative suitability of the\ncandidates to perform the relevant duties, using a competitive\nselection process; and"
    },
