    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-11a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "11A Commissioner’s Directions about employment matters",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-11a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.16",
      "values:originalText": "General\n(1) The Commissioner may issue directions in writing about\nemployment matters relating to APS employees, including the\nfollowing:\n(a) engagement;\n(b) promotion;\n(c) redeployment;\n\n\nThe Australian Public Service  Part 3\n\nSection 12\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024\n(d) mobility;\n(e) training schemes;\n(f) termination.\nNote:\nSee section 42 for general provisions relating to Commissioner’s\nDirections.\nDirections about APS Employment Principles\n(2) The Commissioner may issue directions in writing in relation to\nany of the APS Employment Principles for the purpose of:\n(a) ensuring that the APS incorporates and upholds the APS\nEmployment Principles; and\n(b) determining where necessary the scope or application of the\nAPS Employment Principles.\nNote:\nSee section 42 for general provisions relating to Commissioner’s\nDirections.\n(3) For the purposes of this Act (other than subsection (2)), the APS\nEmployment Principles have effect subject to any restrictions in\ndirections issued under subsection (2).\nDirections of no effect to the extent of inconsistency with Prime\nMinister’s direction\n(4) A direction issued under this section has no effect to the extent that\nit is inconsistent with a direction issued by the Prime Minister\nunder section 21.",
      "skos:definition": "General\n(1) The Commissioner may issue directions in writing about\nemployment matters relating to APS employees, including the\nfollowing:\n(a) engagement;\n(b) promotion;\n(c) redeployment;\n\n\nThe Australian Public Service  Part 3\n\nSection 12\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024\n(d) mobility;\n(e) training schemes;\n(f) termination.\nNote:\nSee section 42 for general provisions relating to Commissioner’s\nDirections.\nDirections about APS Employment Principles\n(2) The Commissioner may issue directions in writing in relation to\nany of the APS Employment Principles for the purpose of:\n(a) ensuring that the APS incorporates and upholds the APS\nEmployment Principles; and\n(b) determining where necessary the scope or application of the\nAPS Employment Principles.\nNote:\nSee section 42 for general provisions relating to Commissioner’s\nDirections.\n(3) For the purposes of this Act (other than subsection (2)), the APS\nEmployment Principles have effect subject to any restrictions in\ndirections issued under subsection (2).\nDirections of no effect to the extent of inconsistency with Prime\nMinister’s direction\n(4) A direction issued under this section has no effect to the extent that\nit is inconsistent with a direction issued by the Prime Minister\nunder section 21.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-11a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-11a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-11a-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-11a-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c910d474dcd724bff83ddedeb06bf1eceaf9fb3af7c76bb282be057f36e6dffa"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-11a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "11A Commissioner’s Directions about employment matters",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 16,
      "values:originalText": "General\n(1) The Commissioner may issue directions in writing about\nemployment matters relating to APS employees, including the\nfollowing:\n(a) engagement;\n(b) promotion;\n(c) redeployment;\n\n\nThe Australian Public Service  Part 3\n\nSection 12\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024\n(d) mobility;\n(e) training schemes;\n(f) termination.\nNote:\nSee section 42 for general provisions relating to Commissioner’s\nDirections.\nDirections about APS Employment Principles\n(2) The Commissioner may issue directions in writing in relation to\nany of the APS Employment Principles for the purpose of:\n(a) ensuring that the APS incorporates and upholds the APS\nEmployment Principles; and\n(b) determining where necessary the scope or application of the\nAPS Employment Principles.\nNote:\nSee section 42 for general provisions relating to Commissioner’s\nDirections.\n(3) For the purposes of this Act (other than subsection (2)), the APS\nEmployment Principles have effect subject to any restrictions in\ndirections issued under subsection (2).\nDirections of no effect to the extent of inconsistency with Prime\nMinister’s direction\n(4) A direction issued under this section has no effect to the extent that\nit is inconsistent with a direction issued by the Prime Minister\nunder section 21."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-11a-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "11A(1) Commissioner’s Directions about employment matters",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-11a-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
