    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-15-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15(5) Breaches of the Code of Conduct",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-15-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.20",
      "values:originalText": "(5) In addition, and without affecting subsection (4), the procedures\nmay be different for:\n(a) different categories of APS employees or former APS\nemployees; or\n(b) APS employees, or former APS employees, who:\n(i) have been convicted of an offence against a\nCommonwealth, State or Territory law in respect of\nconduct that is alleged to constitute a breach of the Code\nof Conduct; or\n(ii) have been found to have committed such an offence but\nno conviction is recorded.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) In addition, and without affecting subsection (4), the procedures\nmay be different for:\n(a) different categories of APS employees or former APS\nemployees; or\n(b) APS employees, or former APS employees, who:\n(i) have been convicted of an offence against a\nCommonwealth, State or Territory law in respect of\nconduct that is alleged to constitute a breach of the Code\nof Conduct; or\n(ii) have been found to have committed such an offence but\nno conviction is recorded.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-15"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-15-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-15-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b1962984ed58b879402d45e8cc4b4fdcd09e52fc758a823e77302daf78fb026e",
      "skos:note": "Procedures for different categories of APS employees or former APS employees may be different."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-15-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15(5) Breaches of the Code of Conduct",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 20,
      "values:originalText": "(5) In addition, and without affecting subsection (4), the procedures\nmay be different for:\n(a) different categories of APS employees or former APS\nemployees; or\n(b) APS employees, or former APS employees, who:\n(i) have been convicted of an offence against a\nCommonwealth, State or Territory law in respect of\nconduct that is alleged to constitute a breach of the Code\nof Conduct; or\n(ii) have been found to have committed such an offence but\nno conviction is recorded."
    },
