    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-19a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "19A Agency Heads to implement measures to create a work",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-19a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.22",
      "values:originalText": "environment that enables decisions to be made by APS\nemployees at lowest appropriate classification\n(1) The Agency Head of an Agency must implement measures that\ncreate a work environment within the Agency that enables\ndecisions to be made by APS employees with classifications that\nthe Agency Head considers are the lowest appropriate for those\ndecisions.\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), an Agency Head must have\nregard to:\n(a) the work level standards for classifications (if any) that are\nreferred to in the Classification Rules; and\n(b) any other matter the Agency Head considers relevant.\n(3) A failure to comply with subsection (1) does not affect the validity\nof a decision.\n\n\nAPS employees  Part 4\nAPS employees generally  Division 1\nSection 20\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024",
      "skos:definition": "environment that enables decisions to be made by APS\nemployees at lowest appropriate classification\n(1) The Agency Head of an Agency must implement measures that\ncreate a work environment within the Agency that enables\ndecisions to be made by APS employees with classifications that\nthe Agency Head considers are the lowest appropriate for those\ndecisions.\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), an Agency Head must have\nregard to:\n(a) the work level standards for classifications (if any) that are\nreferred to in the Classification Rules; and\n(b) any other matter the Agency Head considers relevant.\n(3) A failure to comply with subsection (1) does not affect the validity\nof a decision.\n\n\nAPS employees  Part 4\nAPS employees generally  Division 1\nSection 20\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-19a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-19a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-19a-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bce08e17365a09dd53e7b5003da1bed286eb518a7bf52d54ca93be656aba20e7"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-19a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "19A Agency Heads to implement measures to create a work",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 22,
      "values:originalText": "environment that enables decisions to be made by APS\nemployees at lowest appropriate classification\n(1) The Agency Head of an Agency must implement measures that\ncreate a work environment within the Agency that enables\ndecisions to be made by APS employees with classifications that\nthe Agency Head considers are the lowest appropriate for those\ndecisions.\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), an Agency Head must have\nregard to:\n(a) the work level standards for classifications (if any) that are\nreferred to in the Classification Rules; and\n(b) any other matter the Agency Head considers relevant.\n(3) A failure to comply with subsection (1) does not affect the validity\nof a decision.\n\n\nAPS employees  Part 4\nAPS employees generally  Division 1\nSection 20\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-19a-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "19A(1) Agency Heads to implement measures to create a work",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-19a-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.22",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Agency Head of an Agency must implement measures that\ncreate a work environment within the Agency that enables\ndecisions to be made by APS employees with classifications that\nthe Agency Head considers are the lowest appropriate for those\ndecisions.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Agency Head of an Agency must implement measures that\ncreate a work environment within the Agency that enables\ndecisions to be made by APS employees with classifications that\nthe Agency Head considers are the lowest appropriate for those\ndecisions.",
      "values:partOf": {
