    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-21",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21 Prime Minister’s directions to Agency Heads",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-21"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.23",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Prime Minister may issue general directions in writing to\nAgency Heads relating to the management and leadership of APS\nemployees.\n(2) A direction issued under subsection (1) is a legislative instrument.\nNote:\nSection 42 (disallowance) and Part 4 of Chapter 3 (sunsetting) of the\nLegislation Act 2003 do not apply to the direction (see regulations\nmade for the purposes of paragraphs 44(2)(b) and 54(2)(b) of that\nAct).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Prime Minister may issue general directions in writing to\nAgency Heads relating to the management and leadership of APS\nemployees.\n(2) A direction issued under subsection (1) is a legislative instrument.\nNote:\nSection 42 (disallowance) and Part 4 of Chapter 3 (sunsetting) of the\nLegislation Act 2003 do not apply to the direction (see regulations\nmade for the purposes of paragraphs 44(2)(b) and 54(2)(b) of that\nAct).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-21-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-21-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "80f3f5847a9455221cbb734b55f0067fa853b8dfd9bfbe61cd3fc2ae0dda248c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-21",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "21 Prime Minister’s directions to Agency Heads",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 23,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Prime Minister may issue general directions in writing to\nAgency Heads relating to the management and leadership of APS\nemployees.\n(2) A direction issued under subsection (1) is a legislative instrument.\nNote:\nSection 42 (disallowance) and Part 4 of Chapter 3 (sunsetting) of the\nLegislation Act 2003 do not apply to the direction (see regulations\nmade for the purposes of paragraphs 44(2)(b) and 54(2)(b) of that\nAct)."
    },
