    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-23-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23(4) Classification Rules",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-23-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "(4) An Agency Head may reduce the classification of an APS\nemployee, without the employee’s consent, only in the following\ncircumstances:\n(a) as a sanction under section 15;\n(b) in the case of an SES employee—in accordance with\nCommissioner’s Directions issued under subsection 11A(1);\n(c) on the ground that the employee is excess to the requirements\nof the Agency at the higher classification;\n(d) on the ground that the employee lacks, or has lost, an\nessential qualification for performing duties at the higher\nclassification;\n(e) on the ground of non-performance, or unsatisfactory\nperformance, of duties at the higher classification;\n(f) on the ground that the employee is unable to perform duties\nat the higher classification because of physical or mental\nincapacity;\n(g) in other circumstances prescribed by the regulations.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) An Agency Head may reduce the classification of an APS\nemployee, without the employee’s consent, only in the following\ncircumstances:\n(a) as a sanction under section 15;\n(b) in the case of an SES employee—in accordance with\nCommissioner’s Directions issued under subsection 11A(1);\n(c) on the ground that the employee is excess to the requirements\nof the Agency at the higher classification;\n(d) on the ground that the employee lacks, or has lost, an\nessential qualification for performing duties at the higher\nclassification;\n(e) on the ground of non-performance, or unsatisfactory\nperformance, of duties at the higher classification;\n(f) on the ground that the employee is unable to perform duties\nat the higher classification because of physical or mental\nincapacity;\n(g) in other circumstances prescribed by the regulations.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-23"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-23-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-23-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "18337e33d3a0f46d74fd431372aa6c65aaee28dea03429e6d3d2464448e676bc",
      "skos:note": "Cannot reduce classification without consent in certain circumstances."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-23-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23(4) Classification Rules",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 24,
      "values:originalText": "(4) An Agency Head may reduce the classification of an APS\nemployee, without the employee’s consent, only in the following\ncircumstances:\n(a) as a sanction under section 15;\n(b) in the case of an SES employee—in accordance with\nCommissioner’s Directions issued under subsection 11A(1);\n(c) on the ground that the employee is excess to the requirements\nof the Agency at the higher classification;\n(d) on the ground that the employee lacks, or has lost, an\nessential qualification for performing duties at the higher\nclassification;\n(e) on the ground of non-performance, or unsatisfactory\nperformance, of duties at the higher classification;\n(f) on the ground that the employee is unable to perform duties\nat the higher classification because of physical or mental\nincapacity;\n(g) in other circumstances prescribed by the regulations."
    },
