      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "(5) If a relevant industrial instrument, determination under this Act or\nwritten contract of employment contains procedures to be followed\nwhen reducing the classification, then a reduction is of no effect\nunless those procedures are followed.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) If a relevant industrial instrument, determination under this Act or\nwritten contract of employment contains procedures to be followed\nwhen reducing the classification, then a reduction is of no effect\nunless those procedures are followed.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-23"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-23-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-23-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d7e0760ea334d4606b1ca1302c7fdaabc6ea28073f9e1666f65b3667c1814b21",
      "skos:note": "Procedures must be followed for classification reduction to take effect."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-23-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23(5) Classification Rules",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 24,
      "values:originalText": "(5) If a relevant industrial instrument, determination under this Act or\nwritten contract of employment contains procedures to be followed\nwhen reducing the classification, then a reduction is of no effect\nunless those procedures are followed."
    },
