    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-29",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "29 Termination of employment",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-29"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.28",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An Agency Head may at any time, by notice in writing, terminate\nthe employment of an APS employee in the Agency.\nNote 1:\nThe Fair Work Act 2009 has rules and entitlements that apply to\ntermination of employment.\nNote 2:\nCommissioner’s Directions issued under subsection 11A(1) may set\nout procedures to be followed in terminating the employment of an\nAPS employee.\n(2) For an ongoing APS employee, the notice must specify the ground\nor grounds that are relied on for the termination.\n(3) For an ongoing APS employee, the following are the only grounds\nfor termination:\n(a) the employee is excess to the requirements of the Agency;\n(b) the employee lacks, or has lost, an essential qualification for\nperforming his or her duties;\n(c) non-performance, or unsatisfactory performance, of duties;\n(d) inability to perform duties because of physical or mental\nincapacity;\n(e) failure to satisfactorily complete an entry-level training\ncourse;\n\n\nAPS employees  Part 4\nAPS employees generally  Division 1\nSection 30\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024\n(f) failure to meet a condition imposed under subsection 22(6);\n(g) breach of the Code of Conduct;\n(h) any other ground prescribed by the regulations.\n(4) The regulations may prescribe the grounds for the termination of\nthe employment of non-ongoing APS employees.\n(5) Subsection (4) does not, by implication, limit the grounds for\ntermination of the employment of a non-ongoing APS employee.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An Agency Head may at any time, by notice in writing, terminate\nthe employment of an APS employee in the Agency.\nNote 1:\nThe Fair Work Act 2009 has rules and entitlements that apply to\ntermination of employment.\nNote 2:\nCommissioner’s Directions issued under subsection 11A(1) may set\nout procedures to be followed in terminating the employment of an\nAPS employee.\n(2) For an ongoing APS employee, the notice must specify the ground\nor grounds that are relied on for the termination.\n(3) For an ongoing APS employee, the following are the only grounds\nfor termination:\n(a) the employee is excess to the requirements of the Agency;\n(b) the employee lacks, or has lost, an essential qualification for\nperforming his or her duties;\n(c) non-performance, or unsatisfactory performance, of duties;\n(d) inability to perform duties because of physical or mental\nincapacity;\n(e) failure to satisfactorily complete an entry-level training\ncourse;\n\n\nAPS employees  Part 4\nAPS employees generally  Division 1\nSection 30\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024\n(f) failure to meet a condition imposed under subsection 22(6);\n(g) breach of the Code of Conduct;\n(h) any other ground prescribed by the regulations.\n(4) The regulations may prescribe the grounds for the termination of\nthe employment of non-ongoing APS employees.\n(5) Subsection (4) does not, by implication, limit the grounds for\ntermination of the employment of a non-ongoing APS employee.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-29-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-29-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-29-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-29-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-29-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b2e7d3c8ae359652d496068e55414a628f4c32980e684863207c86811779bc9c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-29",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "29 Termination of employment",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 28,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An Agency Head may at any time, by notice in writing, terminate\nthe employment of an APS employee in the Agency.\nNote 1:\nThe Fair Work Act 2009 has rules and entitlements that apply to\ntermination of employment.\nNote 2:\nCommissioner’s Directions issued under subsection 11A(1) may set\nout procedures to be followed in terminating the employment of an\nAPS employee.\n(2) For an ongoing APS employee, the notice must specify the ground\nor grounds that are relied on for the termination.\n(3) For an ongoing APS employee, the following are the only grounds\nfor termination:\n(a) the employee is excess to the requirements of the Agency;\n(b) the employee lacks, or has lost, an essential qualification for\nperforming his or her duties;\n(c) non-performance, or unsatisfactory performance, of duties;\n(d) inability to perform duties because of physical or mental\nincapacity;\n(e) failure to satisfactorily complete an entry-level training\ncourse;\n\n\nAPS employees  Part 4\nAPS employees generally  Division 1\nSection 30\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024\n(f) failure to meet a condition imposed under subsection 22(6);\n(g) breach of the Code of Conduct;\n(h) any other ground prescribed by the regulations.\n(4) The regulations may prescribe the grounds for the termination of\nthe employment of non-ongoing APS employees.\n(5) Subsection (4) does not, by implication, limit the grounds for\ntermination of the employment of a non-ongoing APS employee."
    },
    {
