    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-31",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "31 Forfeiture of additional remuneration",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-31"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.29",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If an APS employee receives any non-Commonwealth\nremuneration for performing duties as an APS employee, then the\nAgency Head may give a notice in writing to the employee in\nrelation to the whole, or a specified part, of the remuneration.\n(2) The amount notified by the Agency Head:\n(a) is taken to have been received by the employee on behalf of\nthe Commonwealth; and\n(b) may be recovered by the Commonwealth from the employee\nas a debt in a court of competent jurisdiction.\n(3) If an Agency Head receives any non-Commonwealth remuneration\nfor performing duties as an Agency Head, then the Agency\nMinister may give a notice in writing to the Agency Head in\nrelation to the whole, or a specified part, of the remuneration.\n(4) The amount notified by the Agency Minister:",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If an APS employee receives any non-Commonwealth\nremuneration for performing duties as an APS employee, then the\nAgency Head may give a notice in writing to the employee in\nrelation to the whole, or a specified part, of the remuneration.\n(2) The amount notified by the Agency Head:\n(a) is taken to have been received by the employee on behalf of\nthe Commonwealth; and\n(b) may be recovered by the Commonwealth from the employee\nas a debt in a court of competent jurisdiction.\n(3) If an Agency Head receives any non-Commonwealth remuneration\nfor performing duties as an Agency Head, then the Agency\nMinister may give a notice in writing to the Agency Head in\nrelation to the whole, or a specified part, of the remuneration.\n(4) The amount notified by the Agency Minister:",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-31-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-31-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-31-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-31-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a76f91ae88d398cc08c985b06f70a02afd0ab661f70d248896690487bbc99ede"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-31",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "31 Forfeiture of additional remuneration",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 29,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If an APS employee receives any non-Commonwealth\nremuneration for performing duties as an APS employee, then the\nAgency Head may give a notice in writing to the employee in\nrelation to the whole, or a specified part, of the remuneration.\n(2) The amount notified by the Agency Head:\n(a) is taken to have been received by the employee on behalf of\nthe Commonwealth; and\n(b) may be recovered by the Commonwealth from the employee\nas a debt in a court of competent jurisdiction.\n(3) If an Agency Head receives any non-Commonwealth remuneration\nfor performing duties as an Agency Head, then the Agency\nMinister may give a notice in writing to the Agency Head in\nrelation to the whole, or a specified part, of the remuneration.\n(4) The amount notified by the Agency Minister:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-31-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "31(1) Forfeiture of additional remuneration",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-31-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
