    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-33-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "33(6) Review of actions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-33-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.30",
      "values:originalText": "(6) If the Merit Protection Commissioner is not satisfied with the\nresponse to recommendations contained in a report on a review\nunder this section, the Merit Protection Commissioner may, after\nconsulting the Public Service Minister, give a report on the matter\nto the Agency Minister of the responsible Agency and to either or\nboth of the following:\n(a) the Prime Minister;\n(b) the Presiding Officers, for presentation to the Parliament.",
      "skos:definition": "(6) If the Merit Protection Commissioner is not satisfied with the\nresponse to recommendations contained in a report on a review\nunder this section, the Merit Protection Commissioner may, after\nconsulting the Public Service Minister, give a report on the matter\nto the Agency Minister of the responsible Agency and to either or\nboth of the following:\n(a) the Prime Minister;\n(b) the Presiding Officers, for presentation to the Parliament.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-33"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-33-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-33-ss-6-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bc2233b38a96b0a67c8cacb21ab0f4e16aa3c0cd740172380ab3f58317fa2b1d",
      "skos:note": "Must report to Agency Minister and Prime Minister if not satisfied with response to recommendations.",
      "dc:description": "Report on the matter"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-33-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "33(6) Review of actions",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 30,
      "values:originalText": "(6) If the Merit Protection Commissioner is not satisfied with the\nresponse to recommendations contained in a report on a review\nunder this section, the Merit Protection Commissioner may, after\nconsulting the Public Service Minister, give a report on the matter\nto the Agency Minister of the responsible Agency and to either or\nboth of the following:\n(a) the Prime Minister;\n(b) the Presiding Officers, for presentation to the Parliament."
    },
