      "cof:title": "35(3) Constitution and role of SES",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 33,
      "values:originalText": "(3) For the purpose of carrying out the function of the SES, each SES\nemployee:\n(a) provides one or more of the following at a high level:\n(i) professional or specialist expertise;\n(ii) policy advice;\n(iii) program or service delivery;\n(iv) regulatory administration; and\n(b) promotes cooperation within and between Agencies,\nincluding to deliver outcomes across Agency and portfolio\nboundaries; and\n(c) by personal example and other appropriate means, promotes\nthe APS Values, the APS Employment Principles and\ncompliance with the Code of Conduct."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-35-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-35-ss-3"
