      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(i) professional or specialist expertise; (ii) policy advice; (iii) program or service delivery; (iv) regulatory administration"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-37",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "37 Incentive to retire",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-37"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.33",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An Agency Head may give a notice in writing to an SES employee\nin the Agency, stating that the employee will become entitled to a\npayment of a specified amount if the employee retires within a\nperiod specified in the notice.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An Agency Head may give a notice in writing to an SES employee\nin the Agency, stating that the employee will become entitled to a\npayment of a specified amount if the employee retires within a\nperiod specified in the notice.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-37-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-37-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "44c71988a961be49f4e10104846ba6607e579ba0eafe53d0b267274f10d7bd34",
      "skos:note": "Agency Head must provide written notice of retirement payment to SES employee.",
      "dc:description": "true"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-37",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "37 Incentive to retire",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 33,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An Agency Head may give a notice in writing to an SES employee\nin the Agency, stating that the employee will become entitled to a\npayment of a specified amount if the employee retires within a\nperiod specified in the notice."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-37-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-37"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-37-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Agency Head has an obligation to provide notice.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-38",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "38 Commissioner’s certificate required for termination of SES",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-38"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.34",
      "values:originalText": "employment\nAn Agency Head cannot terminate the employment of an SES\nemployee unless the Commissioner has issued a certificate stating\nthat:\n(a) all relevant requirements of Commissioner’s Directions made\nunder subsection 11A(1) have been satisfied in respect of the\nproposed termination; and\n(b) the Commissioner is of the opinion that the termination is in\nthe public interest.\n\n\nAPS employees  Part 4\nHeads of Mission  Division 3\nSection 39\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024",
      "skos:definition": "employment\nAn Agency Head cannot terminate the employment of an SES\nemployee unless the Commissioner has issued a certificate stating\nthat:\n(a) all relevant requirements of Commissioner’s Directions made\nunder subsection 11A(1) have been satisfied in respect of the\nproposed termination; and\n(b) the Commissioner is of the opinion that the termination is in\nthe public interest.\n\n\nAPS employees  Part 4\nHeads of Mission  Division 3\nSection 39\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-38-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-38-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fd547de232b42d1fdcc0cf56fb2249cf303f710effcb588c6f89324c4a9d5b71",
      "skos:note": "Commissioner's certificate required for termination of SES employee"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-38",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "38 Commissioner’s certificate required for termination of SES",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 34,
      "values:originalText": "employment\nAn Agency Head cannot terminate the employment of an SES\nemployee unless the Commissioner has issued a certificate stating\nthat:\n(a) all relevant requirements of Commissioner’s Directions made\nunder subsection 11A(1) have been satisfied in respect of the\nproposed termination; and\n(b) the Commissioner is of the opinion that the termination is in\nthe public interest.\n\n\nAPS employees  Part 4\nHeads of Mission  Division 3\nSection 39\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-38-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-38"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-38-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "requires",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Requires Commissioner's certificate",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-39",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "39 Heads of Mission",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-39"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.35",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The appointment of a Head of Mission by the Governor-General\ncannot take effect unless the person is an APS employee.\n(2) An Agency Head must comply with any direction in writing by the\nAgency Minister:\n(a) directing the Agency Head to engage a particular person as\nan APS employee so that the person can become a Head of\nMission; or\n(b) directing the Agency Head to assign particular duties to an\nAPS employee who has been appointed as a Head of\nMission.\n(3) The APS Employment Principles do not apply to giving, or\ncarrying out, a direction referred to in subsection (2).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The appointment of a Head of Mission by the Governor-General\ncannot take effect unless the person is an APS employee.\n(2) An Agency Head must comply with any direction in writing by the\nAgency Minister:\n(a) directing the Agency Head to engage a particular person as\nan APS employee so that the person can become a Head of\nMission; or\n(b) directing the Agency Head to assign particular duties to an\nAPS employee who has been appointed as a Head of\nMission.\n(3) The APS Employment Principles do not apply to giving, or\ncarrying out, a direction referred to in subsection (2).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-39-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-39-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-39-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ed163e4dad7ecb1399e8451d37aacb6815808d67a043ddaca74b07c5e114b1f4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-39",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "39 Heads of Mission",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 35,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The appointment of a Head of Mission by the Governor-General\ncannot take effect unless the person is an APS employee.\n(2) An Agency Head must comply with any direction in writing by the\nAgency Minister:\n(a) directing the Agency Head to engage a particular person as\nan APS employee so that the person can become a Head of\nMission; or\n(b) directing the Agency Head to assign particular duties to an\nAPS employee who has been appointed as a Head of\nMission.\n(3) The APS Employment Principles do not apply to giving, or\ncarrying out, a direction referred to in subsection (2)."
    },
    {
