      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.40",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Prime Minister may make a request under paragraph (1)(a) in\nrelation to an alleged breach of the Code of Conduct of which the\nPrime Minister has become aware as a result of, or in the course of,\na systems review or a special review.\nProcedures for inquiry",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The Prime Minister may make a request under paragraph (1)(a) in\nrelation to an alleged breach of the Code of Conduct of which the\nPrime Minister has become aware as a result of, or in the course of,\na systems review or a special review.\nProcedures for inquiry",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-41b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-41b-ss-2-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9b8f27a6c3b62082ee7cf45c9d495774d6ce573dc7f8e9196b0b22caef1f9315",
      "skos:note": "Request for inquiry into alleged breach of Code of Conduct"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-41b-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41B(2) Inquiry into alleged breach of Code of Conduct by APS",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 40,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Prime Minister may make a request under paragraph (1)(a) in\nrelation to an alleged breach of the Code of Conduct of which the\nPrime Minister has become aware as a result of, or in the course of,\na systems review or a special review.\nProcedures for inquiry"
    },
    {
