        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-41b-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41B(3) Inquiry into alleged breach of Code of Conduct by APS",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-41b-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.40",
      "values:originalText": "(3) The Commissioner must establish written procedures for inquiring\ninto and determining whether an APS employee, or a former APS\nemployee, in an Agency has breached the Code of Conduct\n(including by engaging in conduct referred to in\nsubsection 15(2A)). The procedures:\n(a) must comply with basic procedural requirements prescribed\nby the regulations; and\n(b) must have due regard to procedural fairness.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) The Commissioner must establish written procedures for inquiring\ninto and determining whether an APS employee, or a former APS\nemployee, in an Agency has breached the Code of Conduct\n(including by engaging in conduct referred to in\nsubsection 15(2A)). The procedures:\n(a) must comply with basic procedural requirements prescribed\nby the regulations; and\n(b) must have due regard to procedural fairness.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-41b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-41b-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-41b-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "656572e96b3171be54583819b841b2229d3f8de1aa5940eeaa7c0a3c7d4bdb7c",
      "skos:note": "Establish written procedures for inquiring into alleged breach of Code of Conduct by APS employees."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-41b-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41B(3) Inquiry into alleged breach of Code of Conduct by APS",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 40,
      "values:originalText": "(3) The Commissioner must establish written procedures for inquiring\ninto and determining whether an APS employee, or a former APS\nemployee, in an Agency has breached the Code of Conduct\n(including by engaging in conduct referred to in\nsubsection 15(2A)). The procedures:\n(a) must comply with basic procedural requirements prescribed\nby the regulations; and\n(b) must have due regard to procedural fairness."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-41b-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-41b-ss-3"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-41b-ss-3-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Duty to establish procedures",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-41b-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41B(4) Inquiry into alleged breach of Code of Conduct by APS",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-41b-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.40",
      "values:originalText": "(4) In addition, and without affecting subsection (3), the procedures\nmay be different for:\n(a) different categories of APS employees or former APS\nemployees; or\n(b) APS employees, or former APS employees, who:\n(i) have been convicted of an offence against a\nCommonwealth, State or Territory law in respect of\n\n\nThe Australian Public Service Commissioner  Part 5\nCommissioner’s functions etc.  Division 1\nSection 41B\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024\nconduct that is alleged to constitute a breach of the Code\nof Conduct; or\n(ii) have been found to have committed such an offence but\nno conviction is recorded.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) In addition, and without affecting subsection (3), the procedures\nmay be different for:\n(a) different categories of APS employees or former APS\nemployees; or\n(b) APS employees, or former APS employees, who:\n(i) have been convicted of an offence against a\nCommonwealth, State or Territory law in respect of\n\n\nThe Australian Public Service Commissioner  Part 5\nCommissioner’s functions etc.  Division 1\nSection 41B\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024\nconduct that is alleged to constitute a breach of the Code\nof Conduct; or\n(ii) have been found to have committed such an offence but\nno conviction is recorded.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-41b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-41b-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-41b-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-41b-ss-4-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-41b-ss-4-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-41b-ss-4-logic-deontic-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ab6732c8a382481495f06cadef5460b4d2961f07feeb9a9a1d7955765eaf0b06",
      "skos:note": "Procedures for inquiry into alleged breach of Code of Conduct may differ based on categories or circumstances."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-41b-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41B(4) Inquiry into alleged breach of Code of Conduct by APS",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 40,
      "values:originalText": "(4) In addition, and without affecting subsection (3), the procedures\nmay be different for:\n(a) different categories of APS employees or former APS\nemployees; or\n(b) APS employees, or former APS employees, who:\n(i) have been convicted of an offence against a\nCommonwealth, State or Territory law in respect of\n\n\nThe Australian Public Service Commissioner  Part 5\nCommissioner’s functions etc.  Division 1\nSection 41B\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024\nconduct that is alleged to constitute a breach of the Code\nof Conduct; or\n(ii) have been found to have committed such an offence but\nno conviction is recorded."
    },
