      "cml:integrityHash": "5460ca8f5df43d1558f4c8e78b42114b29b2a668b8495d397ba17eacfbaf43b9",
      "skos:note": "Notify Agency Head, appoint persons for review, and consult Minister.",
      "dc:description": "Notification, appointment of reviewers, consultation with Minister"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-44a-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44A(4) Capability reviews",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 45,
      "values:originalText": "(4) If a person causes a capability review of an Agency to be\nundertaken under subsection (1) or (3), the person must:\n(a) notify the Agency Head of the Agency, in writing, of the\nreview; and\n(b) appoint one or more persons, in writing, to undertake the\nreview; and\n(ba) ensure that the person or persons who undertake the review\nconsult the Agency Minister of the Agency in undertaking\nthe review; and"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-44a-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-44a-ss-4"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:NaturalPerson"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: NaturalPerson"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-44a-ss-4-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to notify and consult",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-44b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44B Action plans",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-44b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.48",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n(a) a capability review of an Agency is undertaken under\nsubsection 44A(1) or (3); and\n(b) a written report of the review is given to the Agency Head of\nthe Agency under subparagraph 44A(4)(c)(ii);\nthen the Agency Head must, within 90 days after the report is\ngiven to the Agency Head:\n(c) prepare a written action plan that includes the Agency Head’s\nresponse to the findings included in the report; and\n(d) publish the action plan on an Agency website.\n(2) However, the person who caused the capability review into the\nAgency to be undertaken may, by writing:\n(a) authorise the Agency Head to remove specified material from\nthe copy of the action plan that is published; or\n(b) exempt the Agency Head from publishing the action plan;\nif publishing the material or the action plan (as the case may be)\nwould, or could reasonably be expected to, damage:\n(c) the security of the Commonwealth; or\n(d) the defence of the Commonwealth; or\n(e) the international relations of the Commonwealth.\n\n\nThe Australian Public Service Commissioner  Part 5\nCommissioner’s appointment, conditions etc.  Division 2\nSection 45\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n(a) a capability review of an Agency is undertaken under\nsubsection 44A(1) or (3); and\n(b) a written report of the review is given to the Agency Head of\nthe Agency under subparagraph 44A(4)(c)(ii);\nthen the Agency Head must, within 90 days after the report is\ngiven to the Agency Head:\n(c) prepare a written action plan that includes the Agency Head’s\nresponse to the findings included in the report; and\n(d) publish the action plan on an Agency website.\n(2) However, the person who caused the capability review into the\nAgency to be undertaken may, by writing:\n(a) authorise the Agency Head to remove specified material from\nthe copy of the action plan that is published; or\n(b) exempt the Agency Head from publishing the action plan;\nif publishing the material or the action plan (as the case may be)\nwould, or could reasonably be expected to, damage:\n(c) the security of the Commonwealth; or\n(d) the defence of the Commonwealth; or\n(e) the international relations of the Commonwealth.\n\n\nThe Australian Public Service Commissioner  Part 5\nCommissioner’s appointment, conditions etc.  Division 2\nSection 45\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-44b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-44b-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5ee0391d6231364ece97b02cc272cc7bd14e04e7767ba93f34467d682a2d5e47"
    },
    {
