    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-47",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "47 Removal from office",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-47"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.50",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Governor-General may remove the Commissioner from office\nif each House of the Parliament, in the same session of the\nParliament, presents an address to the Governor-General praying\nfor the removal of the Commissioner on the ground of\nmisbehaviour or physical or mental incapacity.\n(2) The Governor-General must remove the Commissioner from office\nif the Commissioner does any of the following:\n(a) becomes bankrupt;\n(b) applies to take the benefit of any law for the relief of\nbankrupt or insolvent debtors;\n(c) compounds with his or her creditors;\n(d) assigns his or her remuneration for the benefit of his or her\ncreditors.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Governor-General may remove the Commissioner from office\nif each House of the Parliament, in the same session of the\nParliament, presents an address to the Governor-General praying\nfor the removal of the Commissioner on the ground of\nmisbehaviour or physical or mental incapacity.\n(2) The Governor-General must remove the Commissioner from office\nif the Commissioner does any of the following:\n(a) becomes bankrupt;\n(b) applies to take the benefit of any law for the relief of\nbankrupt or insolvent debtors;\n(c) compounds with his or her creditors;\n(d) assigns his or her remuneration for the benefit of his or her\ncreditors.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-47-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-47-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "66f325b7aebf2bc5d946341cd4631073c230e3b3b7e0cf8296e5e6acf3d99302"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-47",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "47 Removal from office",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 50,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Governor-General may remove the Commissioner from office\nif each House of the Parliament, in the same session of the\nParliament, presents an address to the Governor-General praying\nfor the removal of the Commissioner on the ground of\nmisbehaviour or physical or mental incapacity.\n(2) The Governor-General must remove the Commissioner from office\nif the Commissioner does any of the following:\n(a) becomes bankrupt;\n(b) applies to take the benefit of any law for the relief of\nbankrupt or insolvent debtors;\n(c) compounds with his or her creditors;\n(d) assigns his or her remuneration for the benefit of his or her\ncreditors."
    },
