        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "85b41612b22719832b9d34f5d23fa8876989b38c5f5321477cd87fce7e8990da"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-48a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "48A Appointment of Special Commissioners",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 51,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Governor-General may, by written instrument, on the\nrecommendation of the Prime Minister, appoint one or more\nSpecial Commissioners to assist the Commissioner in conducting a\nspecified systems review or special review, or a part of such a\nreview.\n(2) The Prime Minister must not recommend that a person be\nappointed as a Special Commissioner unless the Prime Minister\nhas consulted the Commissioner about the appointment.\n(3) A Special Commissioner may be appointed on a full-time basis or\na part-time basis.\n(4) A Special Commissioner holds office for the period specified in the\ninstrument of appointment."
    },
