    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-48b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "48B Remuneration and other terms and conditions of appointment",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-48b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.51",
      "values:originalText": "Remuneration and allowances\n(1) A Special Commissioner is to be paid the remuneration that is\ndetermined by the Remuneration Tribunal. If no determination of\nthat remuneration by the Tribunal is in operation, a Special\nCommissioner is to be paid the remuneration that is prescribed by\nthe regulations.\n(2) A Special Commissioner is to be paid the allowances that are\nprescribed by the regulations.\n(3) Subsections (1) and (2) have effect subject to the Remuneration\nTribunal Act 1973.",
      "skos:definition": "Remuneration and allowances\n(1) A Special Commissioner is to be paid the remuneration that is\ndetermined by the Remuneration Tribunal. If no determination of\nthat remuneration by the Tribunal is in operation, a Special\nCommissioner is to be paid the remuneration that is prescribed by\nthe regulations.\n(2) A Special Commissioner is to be paid the allowances that are\nprescribed by the regulations.\n(3) Subsections (1) and (2) have effect subject to the Remuneration\nTribunal Act 1973.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-48b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-48b-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-48b-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c821f4c86583848f418eb6237204d46ef3f7a31c0e8c47f1f2e936b7ab2da8e3"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-48b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "48B Remuneration and other terms and conditions of appointment",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 51,
      "values:originalText": "Remuneration and allowances\n(1) A Special Commissioner is to be paid the remuneration that is\ndetermined by the Remuneration Tribunal. If no determination of\nthat remuneration by the Tribunal is in operation, a Special\nCommissioner is to be paid the remuneration that is prescribed by\nthe regulations.\n(2) A Special Commissioner is to be paid the allowances that are\nprescribed by the regulations.\n(3) Subsections (1) and (2) have effect subject to the Remuneration\nTribunal Act 1973."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-48b-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "48B(1) Remuneration and other terms and conditions of appointment",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-48b-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.51",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A Special Commissioner is to be paid the remuneration that is\ndetermined by the Remuneration Tribunal. If no determination of\nthat remuneration by the Tribunal is in operation, a Special\nCommissioner is to be paid the remuneration that is prescribed by\nthe regulations.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A Special Commissioner is to be paid the remuneration that is\ndetermined by the Remuneration Tribunal. If no determination of\nthat remuneration by the Tribunal is in operation, a Special\nCommissioner is to be paid the remuneration that is prescribed by\nthe regulations.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-48b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-48b-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-48b-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "221d11a8b497e3f9d58bca2c914eca339aa79b0ffe83a6a895232ad0ae1b5ed3",
      "skos:note": "Special Commissioner must be paid remuneration determined by the Remuneration Tribunal or prescribed by regulations."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-48b-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "48B(1) Remuneration and other terms and conditions of appointment",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 51,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A Special Commissioner is to be paid the remuneration that is\ndetermined by the Remuneration Tribunal. If no determination of\nthat remuneration by the Tribunal is in operation, a Special\nCommissioner is to be paid the remuneration that is prescribed by\nthe regulations."
    },
