    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-48c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "48C Termination of appointment",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-48c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.52",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Governor-General may, by notice in writing, on the\nrecommendation of the Prime Minister, terminate the appointment\nof a Special Commissioner at any time.\n(2) The Prime Minister must not recommend that the appointment of a\nSpecial Commissioner be terminated unless the Prime Minister has\nconsulted the Commissioner about the termination.\n\n\nThe Merit Protection Commissioner  Part 6\nMerit Protection Commissioner’s functions etc.  Division 1\nSection 49\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Governor-General may, by notice in writing, on the\nrecommendation of the Prime Minister, terminate the appointment\nof a Special Commissioner at any time.\n(2) The Prime Minister must not recommend that the appointment of a\nSpecial Commissioner be terminated unless the Prime Minister has\nconsulted the Commissioner about the termination.\n\n\nThe Merit Protection Commissioner  Part 6\nMerit Protection Commissioner’s functions etc.  Division 1\nSection 49\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-48c-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-48c-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "edd75f60f953d63791f27c35d03fc960cd21a25e06a1a69af1e8931ddb32ee4e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-48c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "48C Termination of appointment",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 52,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Governor-General may, by notice in writing, on the\nrecommendation of the Prime Minister, terminate the appointment\nof a Special Commissioner at any time.\n(2) The Prime Minister must not recommend that the appointment of a\nSpecial Commissioner be terminated unless the Prime Minister has\nconsulted the Commissioner about the termination.\n\n\nThe Merit Protection Commissioner  Part 6\nMerit Protection Commissioner’s functions etc.  Division 1\nSection 49\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024"
    },
