    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-57",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "57 Roles and responsibilities of Secretaries",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-57"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.59",
      "values:originalText": "Roles of Secretaries\n(1) The roles of the Secretary of a Department include, but are not\nlimited to, the following:\n(a) principal official policy adviser to the Agency Minister;\n(b) manager, ensuring delivery of government programs and\ncollaboration to achieve outcomes within the Agency\nMinister’s portfolio and, with other Secretaries, across the\nwhole of Government;\n(c) leader, providing stewardship within the Department and, in\npartnership with the Secretaries Board, across the APS;\n(d) any other role prescribed by the regulations.\nResponsibilities of Secretaries\n(2) The responsibilities of the Secretary of a Department are as\nfollows:",
      "skos:definition": "Roles of Secretaries\n(1) The roles of the Secretary of a Department include, but are not\nlimited to, the following:\n(a) principal official policy adviser to the Agency Minister;\n(b) manager, ensuring delivery of government programs and\ncollaboration to achieve outcomes within the Agency\nMinister’s portfolio and, with other Secretaries, across the\nwhole of Government;\n(c) leader, providing stewardship within the Department and, in\npartnership with the Secretaries Board, across the APS;\n(d) any other role prescribed by the regulations.\nResponsibilities of Secretaries\n(2) The responsibilities of the Secretary of a Department are as\nfollows:",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-57-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-57-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "da712b4d79ad49f90bd37896a0190ae53632acd2ba41b9012af00937c7fb70c5"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-57",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "57 Roles and responsibilities of Secretaries",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 59,
      "values:originalText": "Roles of Secretaries\n(1) The roles of the Secretary of a Department include, but are not\nlimited to, the following:\n(a) principal official policy adviser to the Agency Minister;\n(b) manager, ensuring delivery of government programs and\ncollaboration to achieve outcomes within the Agency\nMinister’s portfolio and, with other Secretaries, across the\nwhole of Government;\n(c) leader, providing stewardship within the Department and, in\npartnership with the Secretaries Board, across the APS;\n(d) any other role prescribed by the regulations.\nResponsibilities of Secretaries\n(2) The responsibilities of the Secretary of a Department are as\nfollows:"
    },
