    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-58-ss-8-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The report must be prepared.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Secretary of the Prime Minister’s Department is required to prepare a report.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The report must be prepared after consultation with the Commissioner and the person expected to be the Agency Minister."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-58-ss-8-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "BEGINS",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The consultation must start before the appointment is made.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The person who is expected to be the Agency Minister must be consulted before the appointment is made.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The report must be prepared after the consultation starts."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-58-ss-8-logic-ltl-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "BUT",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The report can be prepared at any time after the consultation starts.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The report from the Secretary of the Prime Minister’s Department is about the appointment of the Secretary of another Department.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The report must be prepared after the consultation starts, but there is no specific deadline."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-58-ss-8-logic-diffusion-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Diffusion"
      },
      "cml:operator": "IS_A",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The report is related to the appointment process.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::diffusion",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The report from the Secretary of the Prime Minister’s Department is about the appointment of the Secretary of another Department.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The report is part of the diffusion of information about the appointment process."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-58-ss-8-logic-cogai-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:CogAI"
      },
      "cml:operator": "IS_A",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The report is a type of artificial intelligence output.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "sparql_library::parsers::chk_parser",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The report from the Secretary of the Prime Minister’s Department is generated by an AI system.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The report is a cogent and coherent piece of information."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-59",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "59 Termination of appointment",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-59"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.62",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Governor-General may, on the recommendation of the Prime\nMinister and by notice in writing, terminate the appointment of a\nSecretary.\nNote:\nIn Barratt v Howard [1999] FCA 1132, the Federal Court of Australia\ndescribed the basis on which requirements of procedural fairness\napplied to the termination of an appointment of Secretary under\nsection 37 of the Public Service Act 1922.\n(2) Before recommending to the Governor-General that the\nappointment of the Secretary of the Prime Minister’s Department\nbe terminated, the Prime Minister must have received a report\nabout the proposed termination from the Commissioner.\n(3) Before recommending to the Governor-General that the\nappointment of the Secretary of a Department other than the Prime\nMinister’s Department be terminated, the Prime Minister must\nhave received a report about the proposed termination from the\nSecretary of the Prime Minister’s Department.\n(4) The report from the Secretary of the Prime Minister’s Department\nabout the proposed termination of the appointment of the Secretary\nof another Department must:\n(a) be prepared after consultation with the Commissioner; and\n(b) if the Secretary of the Prime Minister’s Department and the\nCommissioner disagree in relation to the proposed\ntermination—explain the substance of the disagreement.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Governor-General may, on the recommendation of the Prime\nMinister and by notice in writing, terminate the appointment of a\nSecretary.\nNote:\nIn Barratt v Howard [1999] FCA 1132, the Federal Court of Australia\ndescribed the basis on which requirements of procedural fairness\napplied to the termination of an appointment of Secretary under\nsection 37 of the Public Service Act 1922.\n(2) Before recommending to the Governor-General that the\nappointment of the Secretary of the Prime Minister’s Department\nbe terminated, the Prime Minister must have received a report\nabout the proposed termination from the Commissioner.\n(3) Before recommending to the Governor-General that the\nappointment of the Secretary of a Department other than the Prime\nMinister’s Department be terminated, the Prime Minister must\nhave received a report about the proposed termination from the\nSecretary of the Prime Minister’s Department.\n(4) The report from the Secretary of the Prime Minister’s Department\nabout the proposed termination of the appointment of the Secretary\nof another Department must:\n(a) be prepared after consultation with the Commissioner; and\n(b) if the Secretary of the Prime Minister’s Department and the\nCommissioner disagree in relation to the proposed\ntermination—explain the substance of the disagreement.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-59-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-59-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-59-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-59-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4fdb3d4b250b6aec90d1a35a9d5f8cf561bed0983401437bf0dc7367117dcaac"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-59",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "59 Termination of appointment",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 62,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Governor-General may, on the recommendation of the Prime\nMinister and by notice in writing, terminate the appointment of a\nSecretary.\nNote:\nIn Barratt v Howard [1999] FCA 1132, the Federal Court of Australia\ndescribed the basis on which requirements of procedural fairness\napplied to the termination of an appointment of Secretary under\nsection 37 of the Public Service Act 1922.\n(2) Before recommending to the Governor-General that the\nappointment of the Secretary of the Prime Minister’s Department\nbe terminated, the Prime Minister must have received a report\nabout the proposed termination from the Commissioner.\n(3) Before recommending to the Governor-General that the\nappointment of the Secretary of a Department other than the Prime\nMinister’s Department be terminated, the Prime Minister must\nhave received a report about the proposed termination from the\nSecretary of the Prime Minister’s Department.\n(4) The report from the Secretary of the Prime Minister’s Department\nabout the proposed termination of the appointment of the Secretary\nof another Department must:\n(a) be prepared after consultation with the Commissioner; and\n(b) if the Secretary of the Prime Minister’s Department and the\nCommissioner disagree in relation to the proposed\ntermination—explain the substance of the disagreement."
    },
