    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-61a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "61A Annual performance review",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-61a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.63",
      "values:originalText": "An annual review of the performance of a Secretary must be\ncarried out in accordance with a framework established by the\nSecretary of the Prime Minister’s Department and the\nCommissioner.",
      "skos:definition": "An annual review of the performance of a Secretary must be\ncarried out in accordance with a framework established by the\nSecretary of the Prime Minister’s Department and the\nCommissioner.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-61a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-61a-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "969af2aa27def574e83160bd46b29eb62317f7e16647636031d02b7beade4c54",
      "skos:note": "Annual performance review must be carried out"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-61a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "61A Annual performance review",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 63,
      "values:originalText": "An annual review of the performance of a Secretary must be\ncarried out in accordance with a framework established by the\nSecretary of the Prime Minister’s Department and the\nCommissioner."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-61a-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-61a"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-61a-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to perform annual review",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-62",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "62 Acting Secretary",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-62"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.63",
      "values:originalText": "The Prime Minister may appoint a person to act as the Secretary of\na Department:\n(a) if there is a vacancy in the office of Secretary, whether or not\nan appointment has previously been made to the office; or\n(b) during any period, or during all periods, when the Secretary\nis absent from duty or from Australia or is, for any reason,\nunable to perform the duties of the office.\nNote:\nFor rules that apply to acting appointments, see section 33A of the\nActs Interpretation Act 1901.",
      "skos:definition": "The Prime Minister may appoint a person to act as the Secretary of\na Department:\n(a) if there is a vacancy in the office of Secretary, whether or not\nan appointment has previously been made to the office; or\n(b) during any period, or during all periods, when the Secretary\nis absent from duty or from Australia or is, for any reason,\nunable to perform the duties of the office.\nNote:\nFor rules that apply to acting appointments, see section 33A of the\nActs Interpretation Act 1901.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-62-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-62-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "db64f47f6ae4291f6c020fa8025531e5c747e1a5215fd8fe00ca1a573da02f19",
      "skos:note": "Appoint acting Secretary under certain circumstances.",
      "dc:references": [
        "sec-33A"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-62",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "62 Acting Secretary",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 63,
      "values:originalText": "The Prime Minister may appoint a person to act as the Secretary of\na Department:\n(a) if there is a vacancy in the office of Secretary, whether or not\nan appointment has previously been made to the office; or\n(b) during any period, or during all periods, when the Secretary\nis absent from duty or from Australia or is, for any reason,\nunable to perform the duties of the office.\nNote:\nFor rules that apply to acting appointments, see section 33A of the\nActs Interpretation Act 1901."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-62-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-62"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-62-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "may",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Permission to act as Secretary",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-64",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "64 Secretaries Board",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-64"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.64",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretaries Board is established by this section.\n(2) The Secretaries Board consists of the following members:\n(a) the Secretary of the Prime Minister’s Department, as Chair;\n(b) the Secretary of each other Department;\n(c) the Commissioner;\n(d) such other persons as are nominated in writing by the\nSecretary of the Prime Minister’s Department.\n(3) The Secretaries Board has the following functions:\n(a) to take responsibility for the stewardship of the APS and for\ndeveloping and implementing strategies to improve the APS;\n(b) to identify strategic priorities for the APS and consider issues\nthat affect the APS;\n(c) to set an annual work program, and direct subcommittees to\ndevelop strategies to address APS-wide issues and make\nrecommendations to the Secretaries Board;\n(d) to draw together advice from senior leaders in government,\nbusiness and the community;\n(e) to work collaboratively and model leadership behaviours;\n(f) such other functions as are conferred on the Secretaries\nBoard by this Act.\n(4) The Secretaries Board may establish one or more senior leadership\ngroups, consisting of members determined by the Secretaries\nBoard, to assist the Secretaries Board in performing its functions.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Secretaries Board is established by this section.\n(2) The Secretaries Board consists of the following members:\n(a) the Secretary of the Prime Minister’s Department, as Chair;\n(b) the Secretary of each other Department;\n(c) the Commissioner;\n(d) such other persons as are nominated in writing by the\nSecretary of the Prime Minister’s Department.\n(3) The Secretaries Board has the following functions:\n(a) to take responsibility for the stewardship of the APS and for\ndeveloping and implementing strategies to improve the APS;\n(b) to identify strategic priorities for the APS and consider issues\nthat affect the APS;\n(c) to set an annual work program, and direct subcommittees to\ndevelop strategies to address APS-wide issues and make\nrecommendations to the Secretaries Board;\n(d) to draw together advice from senior leaders in government,\nbusiness and the community;\n(e) to work collaboratively and model leadership behaviours;\n(f) such other functions as are conferred on the Secretaries\nBoard by this Act.\n(4) The Secretaries Board may establish one or more senior leadership\ngroups, consisting of members determined by the Secretaries\nBoard, to assist the Secretaries Board in performing its functions.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-64-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-64-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-64-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-64-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "266400da352f5338837bc3b9cd54e77b3ab890e29b0957f655784f3fd500d914"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-64",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "64 Secretaries Board",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 64,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretaries Board is established by this section.\n(2) The Secretaries Board consists of the following members:\n(a) the Secretary of the Prime Minister’s Department, as Chair;\n(b) the Secretary of each other Department;\n(c) the Commissioner;\n(d) such other persons as are nominated in writing by the\nSecretary of the Prime Minister’s Department.\n(3) The Secretaries Board has the following functions:\n(a) to take responsibility for the stewardship of the APS and for\ndeveloping and implementing strategies to improve the APS;\n(b) to identify strategic priorities for the APS and consider issues\nthat affect the APS;\n(c) to set an annual work program, and direct subcommittees to\ndevelop strategies to address APS-wide issues and make\nrecommendations to the Secretaries Board;\n(d) to draw together advice from senior leaders in government,\nbusiness and the community;\n(e) to work collaboratively and model leadership behaviours;\n(f) such other functions as are conferred on the Secretaries\nBoard by this Act.\n(4) The Secretaries Board may establish one or more senior leadership\ngroups, consisting of members determined by the Secretaries\nBoard, to assist the Secretaries Board in performing its functions."
    },
