    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-64a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "64A Long-term insights reports",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-64a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.64",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretaries Board may cause long-term insights reports to be\nprepared in relation to one or more matters of public policy.\n\n\nSecretaries Board  Part 8\n\nSection 64A\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024\n(2) The purpose of a long-term insights report is to make available:\n(a) information about medium-term and long-term trends, risks,\nand opportunities that affect or may affect Australia or\nAustralian society; and\n(b) information and impartial analysis relating to those trends,\nrisks and opportunities.\n(3) The preparation of a long-term insights report must make provision\nfor public consultation.\n(3A) As soon as practicable after a long-term insights report has been\ncompleted, the Secretaries Board must give the report to the Public\nService Minister.\n(3B) The Public Service Minister must cause a copy of a long-term\ninsights report to be tabled in each House of the Parliament within\n15 sitting days of that House after the report is given to the\nMinister.\n(4) As soon as practicable after a long-term insights report has been\ngiven to the Public Service Minister, the report must be published,\nin the manner and form the Secretaries Board considers\nappropriate:\n(a) on an Agency website; and\n(b) if the Secretaries Board considers appropriate—elsewhere.\n(5) An Agency may assist in the preparation of a long-term insights\nreport.\n(6) The Secretaries Board must cause at least one long-term insights\nreport to be prepared each financial year.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Secretaries Board may cause long-term insights reports to be\nprepared in relation to one or more matters of public policy.\n\n\nSecretaries Board  Part 8\n\nSection 64A\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024\n(2) The purpose of a long-term insights report is to make available:\n(a) information about medium-term and long-term trends, risks,\nand opportunities that affect or may affect Australia or\nAustralian society; and\n(b) information and impartial analysis relating to those trends,\nrisks and opportunities.\n(3) The preparation of a long-term insights report must make provision\nfor public consultation.\n(3A) As soon as practicable after a long-term insights report has been\ncompleted, the Secretaries Board must give the report to the Public\nService Minister.\n(3B) The Public Service Minister must cause a copy of a long-term\ninsights report to be tabled in each House of the Parliament within\n15 sitting days of that House after the report is given to the\nMinister.\n(4) As soon as practicable after a long-term insights report has been\ngiven to the Public Service Minister, the report must be published,\nin the manner and form the Secretaries Board considers\nappropriate:\n(a) on an Agency website; and\n(b) if the Secretaries Board considers appropriate—elsewhere.\n(5) An Agency may assist in the preparation of a long-term insights\nreport.\n(6) The Secretaries Board must cause at least one long-term insights\nreport to be prepared each financial year.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-64a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-64a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-64a-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-64a-ss-3a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-64a-ss-3b"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-64a-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-64a-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-64a-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "03a9fb0f726202a81adcd55b81869b18312c15a29cd9c96613b5478c2c96b62f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-64a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "64A Long-term insights reports",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 64,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretaries Board may cause long-term insights reports to be\nprepared in relation to one or more matters of public policy.\n\n\nSecretaries Board  Part 8\n\nSection 64A\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024\n(2) The purpose of a long-term insights report is to make available:\n(a) information about medium-term and long-term trends, risks,\nand opportunities that affect or may affect Australia or\nAustralian society; and\n(b) information and impartial analysis relating to those trends,\nrisks and opportunities.\n(3) The preparation of a long-term insights report must make provision\nfor public consultation.\n(3A) As soon as practicable after a long-term insights report has been\ncompleted, the Secretaries Board must give the report to the Public\nService Minister.\n(3B) The Public Service Minister must cause a copy of a long-term\ninsights report to be tabled in each House of the Parliament within\n15 sitting days of that House after the report is given to the\nMinister.\n(4) As soon as practicable after a long-term insights report has been\ngiven to the Public Service Minister, the report must be published,\nin the manner and form the Secretaries Board considers\nappropriate:\n(a) on an Agency website; and\n(b) if the Secretaries Board considers appropriate—elsewhere.\n(5) An Agency may assist in the preparation of a long-term insights\nreport.\n(6) The Secretaries Board must cause at least one long-term insights\nreport to be prepared each financial year."
    },
