    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-65",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "65 Establishment etc. of Executive Agencies",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-65"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.66",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Governor-General may do any of the following, by order in\nthe Gazette:\n(a) establish or abolish an Executive Agency;\n(b) allocate a name to an Executive Agency or the Head of an\nExecutive Agency;\n(c) identify the Minister who is responsible for an Executive\nAgency;\n(d) specify the functions of an Executive Agency.\n(2) For the purposes of this Act, an Executive Agency consists of the\nHead of the Agency, together with the APS employees assisting\nthe Head.\n(3) When an Executive Agency is established, an office of Head of the\nAgency is established by force of this subsection. The name of the\noffice is “Head of the [name of Agency]”, unless the office of Head\nhas a different name because of an order under subsection (1).\n(4) When an Executive Agency is abolished, the office of Head of the\nAgency is abolished by force of this subsection.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Governor-General may do any of the following, by order in\nthe Gazette:\n(a) establish or abolish an Executive Agency;\n(b) allocate a name to an Executive Agency or the Head of an\nExecutive Agency;\n(c) identify the Minister who is responsible for an Executive\nAgency;\n(d) specify the functions of an Executive Agency.\n(2) For the purposes of this Act, an Executive Agency consists of the\nHead of the Agency, together with the APS employees assisting\nthe Head.\n(3) When an Executive Agency is established, an office of Head of the\nAgency is established by force of this subsection. The name of the\noffice is “Head of the [name of Agency]”, unless the office of Head\nhas a different name because of an order under subsection (1).\n(4) When an Executive Agency is abolished, the office of Head of the\nAgency is abolished by force of this subsection.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-65-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-65-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-65-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-65-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4a372bdd6df008d44bf97056942bdd5849358b73d78951c81ae45c6bc95e2a2f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-65",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "65 Establishment etc. of Executive Agencies",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 66,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Governor-General may do any of the following, by order in\nthe Gazette:\n(a) establish or abolish an Executive Agency;\n(b) allocate a name to an Executive Agency or the Head of an\nExecutive Agency;\n(c) identify the Minister who is responsible for an Executive\nAgency;\n(d) specify the functions of an Executive Agency.\n(2) For the purposes of this Act, an Executive Agency consists of the\nHead of the Agency, together with the APS employees assisting\nthe Head.\n(3) When an Executive Agency is established, an office of Head of the\nAgency is established by force of this subsection. The name of the\noffice is “Head of the [name of Agency]”, unless the office of Head\nhas a different name because of an order under subsection (1).\n(4) When an Executive Agency is abolished, the office of Head of the\nAgency is abolished by force of this subsection."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-65-ss-1",
