    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-66",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "66 Responsibilities of Heads of Executive Agencies",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-66"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.66",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Head of an Executive Agency, under the Agency Minister, is\nresponsible for managing the Agency.\n(2) The Head of an Executive Agency must assist the Agency Minister\nto fulfil the Agency Minister’s accountability obligations to the\nParliament to provide factual information, as required by the\nParliament, in relation to the operation and administration of the\nAgency.\n\n\nExecutive Agencies  Part 9\n\nSection 67\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024\n(3) The Head of an Executive Agency is accountable to the\ngovernment, the Parliament and the public in the same way as the\nSecretary of a Department.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Head of an Executive Agency, under the Agency Minister, is\nresponsible for managing the Agency.\n(2) The Head of an Executive Agency must assist the Agency Minister\nto fulfil the Agency Minister’s accountability obligations to the\nParliament to provide factual information, as required by the\nParliament, in relation to the operation and administration of the\nAgency.\n\n\nExecutive Agencies  Part 9\n\nSection 67\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024\n(3) The Head of an Executive Agency is accountable to the\ngovernment, the Parliament and the public in the same way as the\nSecretary of a Department.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-66-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-66-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-66-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "26aada263b1b199c2406eca17549ad0ecf697ceb8be8ea6b0765fd4f01895fc7"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-66",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "66 Responsibilities of Heads of Executive Agencies",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 66,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Head of an Executive Agency, under the Agency Minister, is\nresponsible for managing the Agency.\n(2) The Head of an Executive Agency must assist the Agency Minister\nto fulfil the Agency Minister’s accountability obligations to the\nParliament to provide factual information, as required by the\nParliament, in relation to the operation and administration of the\nAgency.\n\n\nExecutive Agencies  Part 9\n\nSection 67\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024\n(3) The Head of an Executive Agency is accountable to the\ngovernment, the Parliament and the public in the same way as the\nSecretary of a Department."
    },
