    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-69",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "69 Acting Head",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-69"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.68",
      "values:originalText": "The Agency Minister of an Executive Agency may appoint a\nperson to act as Head of the Agency:\n(a) if there is a vacancy in the office of Head, whether or not an\nappointment has previously been made to the office; or\n(b) during any period, or during all periods, when the Head is\nabsent from duty or from Australia or is, for any reason,\nunable to perform the duties of the office.\nNote:\nFor rules that apply to acting appointments, see section 33A of the\nActs Interpretation Act 1901.\n\n\nAdministrative arrangements and re-organisations  Part 10\n\nSection 71\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024",
      "skos:definition": "The Agency Minister of an Executive Agency may appoint a\nperson to act as Head of the Agency:\n(a) if there is a vacancy in the office of Head, whether or not an\nappointment has previously been made to the office; or\n(b) during any period, or during all periods, when the Head is\nabsent from duty or from Australia or is, for any reason,\nunable to perform the duties of the office.\nNote:\nFor rules that apply to acting appointments, see section 33A of the\nActs Interpretation Act 1901.\n\n\nAdministrative arrangements and re-organisations  Part 10\n\nSection 71\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-69-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1da352c58c29567504cd3a5b3860b6117e38a803a9e93243c5fb9395ae356f29",
      "skos:note": "May appoint a person to act as Head of the Agency under certain circumstances."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-69",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "69 Acting Head",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 68,
      "values:originalText": "The Agency Minister of an Executive Agency may appoint a\nperson to act as Head of the Agency:\n(a) if there is a vacancy in the office of Head, whether or not an\nappointment has previously been made to the office; or\n(b) during any period, or during all periods, when the Head is\nabsent from duty or from Australia or is, for any reason,\nunable to perform the duties of the office.\nNote:\nFor rules that apply to acting appointments, see section 33A of the\nActs Interpretation Act 1901.\n\n\nAdministrative arrangements and re-organisations  Part 10\n\nSection 71\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-69-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-69"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-71",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "71 Arrangements with States and Territories",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-71"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.69",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Prime Minister may arrange with an appropriate authority of a\nState:\n(a) for an APS employee to perform services for the State as an\nAPS employee; or\n(b) for a State employee to perform services in an Agency as a\nState employee.\n(2) In this section:\nState means a State or Territory or an authority of a State or\nTerritory.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Prime Minister may arrange with an appropriate authority of a\nState:\n(a) for an APS employee to perform services for the State as an\nAPS employee; or\n(b) for a State employee to perform services in an Agency as a\nState employee.\n(2) In this section:\nState means a State or Territory or an authority of a State or\nTerritory.",
