    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-72",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "72 Machinery of government changes",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-72"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.69",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commissioner may do any of the following, if the\nCommissioner is satisfied that it is necessary or desirable in order\nto give effect to an administrative re-arrangement:\n(a) move APS employees to another Agency (without anyone’s\nconsent), by a determination in writing;\n(b) determine in writing that APS employees cease to be APS\nemployees and become non-APS employees of a specified\nCommonwealth body or Commonwealth authority;\n(c) determine in writing that non-APS employees cease to be\nemployed as non-APS employees and become engaged as\nAPS employees in a specified Agency;\n(d) on behalf of the Commonwealth, engage any person as an\nAPS employee in a specified Agency.\n(2) A determination by the Commissioner has effect according to its\nterms, by force of this section.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commissioner may do any of the following, if the\nCommissioner is satisfied that it is necessary or desirable in order\nto give effect to an administrative re-arrangement:\n(a) move APS employees to another Agency (without anyone’s\nconsent), by a determination in writing;\n(b) determine in writing that APS employees cease to be APS\nemployees and become non-APS employees of a specified\nCommonwealth body or Commonwealth authority;\n(c) determine in writing that non-APS employees cease to be\nemployed as non-APS employees and become engaged as\nAPS employees in a specified Agency;\n(d) on behalf of the Commonwealth, engage any person as an\nAPS employee in a specified Agency.\n(2) A determination by the Commissioner has effect according to its\nterms, by force of this section.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-72-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-72-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f28c4aecfb1e2bbdb92b5d642673762c248df2b0efd8016df9f499724c7c94d2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-72",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "72 Machinery of government changes",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 69,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commissioner may do any of the following, if the\nCommissioner is satisfied that it is necessary or desirable in order\nto give effect to an administrative re-arrangement:\n(a) move APS employees to another Agency (without anyone’s\nconsent), by a determination in writing;\n(b) determine in writing that APS employees cease to be APS\nemployees and become non-APS employees of a specified\nCommonwealth body or Commonwealth authority;\n(c) determine in writing that non-APS employees cease to be\nemployed as non-APS employees and become engaged as\nAPS employees in a specified Agency;\n(d) on behalf of the Commonwealth, engage any person as an\nAPS employee in a specified Agency.\n(2) A determination by the Commissioner has effect according to its\nterms, by force of this section."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-72-ss-1",
