          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-72b-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-72b-ss-4-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b0d485ffbd7579a993e9cbc573f91cff72f20f9f9fa76b3b470a475fc0a5c5ff",
      "skos:note": "Disclosure of protected information for report purposes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-72b-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "72B(4) Protection of information—Merit Protection Commissioner’s",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 74,
      "values:originalText": "(4) The Merit Protection Commissioner may disclose protected\ninformation in a report prepared for purposes connected with the\nperformance of the functions, or the exercise of the powers, of the\nMerit Protection Commissioner under this Act or the regulations, if\nthe Merit Protection Commissioner is satisfied that the disclosure\nis necessary for the purpose of setting out the grounds for the\nconclusions and recommendations contained in the report."
    },
