    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-72d",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "72D Giving information or producing documents to Merit",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-72d"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.79",
      "values:originalText": "Protection Commissioner not admissible in evidence etc.\nApplication\n(1) This section applies if:\n(a) either:\n(i) the Merit Protection Commissioner requests a person to\ngive information (including an answer to a question) or\nproduce a document to the Merit Protection\nCommissioner for purposes connected with the\nperformance of functions or duties, or the exercise of\npowers, under a provision referred to in subsection (2);\nor\n(ii) a person reasonably believes that information or a\ndocument is relevant for purposes connected with the\nperformance of functions or duties, or the exercise of\npowers, under a provision referred to in subsection (2);\nand\n(b) the person obtained the information or document lawfully;\nand\n(c) the person gives the information or produces the document to\nthe Merit Protection Commissioner.\n(2) For the purposes of subparagraphs (1)(a)(i) and (ii), the provisions\nare:\n(a) sections 50 and 50A; and\n(b) any other provision of this Act or the regulations prescribed\nby the regulations for the purposes of this paragraph.\nGiving information or producing document not admissible in\nevidence in certain proceedings\n(3) If, by giving the information or producing the document to the\nMerit Protection Commissioner, the person:\n(a) contravenes any other law; or",
      "skos:definition": "Protection Commissioner not admissible in evidence etc.\nApplication\n(1) This section applies if:\n(a) either:\n(i) the Merit Protection Commissioner requests a person to\ngive information (including an answer to a question) or\nproduce a document to the Merit Protection\nCommissioner for purposes connected with the\nperformance of functions or duties, or the exercise of\npowers, under a provision referred to in subsection (2);\nor\n(ii) a person reasonably believes that information or a\ndocument is relevant for purposes connected with the\nperformance of functions or duties, or the exercise of\npowers, under a provision referred to in subsection (2);\nand\n(b) the person obtained the information or document lawfully;\nand\n(c) the person gives the information or produces the document to\nthe Merit Protection Commissioner.\n(2) For the purposes of subparagraphs (1)(a)(i) and (ii), the provisions\nare:\n(a) sections 50 and 50A; and\n(b) any other provision of this Act or the regulations prescribed\nby the regulations for the purposes of this paragraph.\nGiving information or producing document not admissible in\nevidence in certain proceedings\n(3) If, by giving the information or producing the document to the\nMerit Protection Commissioner, the person:\n(a) contravenes any other law; or",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-72d-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-72d-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-72d-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "392b3757e30e2a84b738d4245dad269cb96452be20a40c517166a116613891cb"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-72d",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "72D Giving information or producing documents to Merit",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 79,
      "values:originalText": "Protection Commissioner not admissible in evidence etc.\nApplication\n(1) This section applies if:\n(a) either:\n(i) the Merit Protection Commissioner requests a person to\ngive information (including an answer to a question) or\nproduce a document to the Merit Protection\nCommissioner for purposes connected with the\nperformance of functions or duties, or the exercise of\npowers, under a provision referred to in subsection (2);\nor\n(ii) a person reasonably believes that information or a\ndocument is relevant for purposes connected with the\nperformance of functions or duties, or the exercise of\npowers, under a provision referred to in subsection (2);\nand\n(b) the person obtained the information or document lawfully;\nand\n(c) the person gives the information or produces the document to\nthe Merit Protection Commissioner.\n(2) For the purposes of subparagraphs (1)(a)(i) and (ii), the provisions\nare:\n(a) sections 50 and 50A; and\n(b) any other provision of this Act or the regulations prescribed\nby the regulations for the purposes of this paragraph.\nGiving information or producing document not admissible in\nevidence in certain proceedings\n(3) If, by giving the information or producing the document to the\nMerit Protection Commissioner, the person:\n(a) contravenes any other law; or"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-72d-ss-1",
