    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-72e",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "72E Release of personal information",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-72e"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.80",
      "values:originalText": "The regulations:\n\n\nProtection of information  Part 10A\n\nSection 72E\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024\n(a) may authorise the use or disclosure, in specific\ncircumstances, of personal information (within the meaning\nof the Privacy Act 1988); and\n(b) may impose restrictions on the collection, storage, access,\nfurther use or further disclosure of personal information used\nor disclosed under regulations made for the purposes of\nparagraph (a).\nNote:\nThe Freedom of Information Act 1982 and the Privacy Act 1988 have\nrules about the use and disclosure of personal information.",
      "skos:definition": "The regulations:\n\n\nProtection of information  Part 10A\n\nSection 72E\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024\n(a) may authorise the use or disclosure, in specific\ncircumstances, of personal information (within the meaning\nof the Privacy Act 1988); and\n(b) may impose restrictions on the collection, storage, access,\nfurther use or further disclosure of personal information used\nor disclosed under regulations made for the purposes of\nparagraph (a).\nNote:\nThe Freedom of Information Act 1982 and the Privacy Act 1988 have\nrules about the use and disclosure of personal information.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-72e-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-72e-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cf1445b90742a0159e38333cdf0aca588ef588016b7c7b828125455f7be6a194",
      "skos:note": "Authorises use or disclosure of personal information in specific circumstances."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-72e",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "72E Release of personal information",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 80,
      "values:originalText": "The regulations:\n\n\nProtection of information  Part 10A\n\nSection 72E\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024\n(a) may authorise the use or disclosure, in specific\ncircumstances, of personal information (within the meaning\nof the Privacy Act 1988); and\n(b) may impose restrictions on the collection, storage, access,\nfurther use or further disclosure of personal information used\nor disclosed under regulations made for the purposes of\nparagraph (a).\nNote:\nThe Freedom of Information Act 1982 and the Privacy Act 1988 have\nrules about the use and disclosure of personal information."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-72e-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-72e"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-72e-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "authorise",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Imposes permission",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-73",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "73 Payments in special circumstances",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/public-service-act-1999#sec-73"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "public-service-act-1999.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "public-service-act-1999.pdf, p.82",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Public Service Minister may authorise the making of payments\nto a person under subsection (2) if the Public Service Minister\nconsiders it appropriate to do so because of special circumstances\nthat relate to, or arise out of:\n(a) the payee’s employment by the Commonwealth; or\n(b) another person’s employment by the Commonwealth.\n(2) The Public Service Minister may authorise the making of any of\nthe following payments:\n(a) one or more payments of an amount or amounts specified in\nthe authorisation (or worked out in accordance with the\nauthorisation);\n(b) periodical payments of an amount specified in the\nauthorisation (or worked out in accordance with the\nauthorisation), during a period specified in the authorisation\n(or worked out in accordance with the authorisation).\n(3) Payments may be authorised under this section even though the\npayments would not otherwise be authorised by law or required to\nmeet a legal liability.\n(4) An authorisation cannot be made under this section if it would\ninvolve, or be likely to involve, a total amount exceeding the\namount prescribed by the regulations.\n(5) Conditions may be attached to payments under this section. If a\ncondition is breached, the payment may be recovered by the\nCommonwealth as a debt in a court of competent jurisdiction.\nNote:\nPayments under this section must be made from money appropriated\nby the Parliament. Generally, a payment can be debited against an\nAgency’s annual appropriation, providing that it relates to some\nmatter that has arisen in the course of its administration.\n\n\nMiscellaneous  Part 11\n\nSection 74\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Public Service Minister may authorise the making of payments\nto a person under subsection (2) if the Public Service Minister\nconsiders it appropriate to do so because of special circumstances\nthat relate to, or arise out of:\n(a) the payee’s employment by the Commonwealth; or\n(b) another person’s employment by the Commonwealth.\n(2) The Public Service Minister may authorise the making of any of\nthe following payments:\n(a) one or more payments of an amount or amounts specified in\nthe authorisation (or worked out in accordance with the\nauthorisation);\n(b) periodical payments of an amount specified in the\nauthorisation (or worked out in accordance with the\nauthorisation), during a period specified in the authorisation\n(or worked out in accordance with the authorisation).\n(3) Payments may be authorised under this section even though the\npayments would not otherwise be authorised by law or required to\nmeet a legal liability.\n(4) An authorisation cannot be made under this section if it would\ninvolve, or be likely to involve, a total amount exceeding the\namount prescribed by the regulations.\n(5) Conditions may be attached to payments under this section. If a\ncondition is breached, the payment may be recovered by the\nCommonwealth as a debt in a court of competent jurisdiction.\nNote:\nPayments under this section must be made from money appropriated\nby the Parliament. Generally, a payment can be debited against an\nAgency’s annual appropriation, providing that it relates to some\nmatter that has arisen in the course of its administration.\n\n\nMiscellaneous  Part 11\n\nSection 74\nPublic Service Act 1999\nCompilation date: 11/12/2024",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-73-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:public-service-act-1999-sec-73-ss-2"
        },
